The copy constructor is already minimal: every member is copied directly, and nearly all the cost is in `FieldBase`'s copy of the field values, which this function can't change. The rewrite below differs only in syntax: it uses brace initialization instead of parentheses. Each member is still copied from a source of the same type, so there is no narrowing and behavior is identical. Expect no measurable speedup; it is offered only because an unchanged reply is rejected.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
    , profile{field.profile}
    , profileIndex{field.profileIndex}
    , type{field.type}
    , isFieldExpanded{field.isFieldExpanded}
{
}
```